{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1792418429","published":"2026-10-30T15:11:31Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:30:17.144778920Z","upstream":["CVE-2021-47200","CVE-2022-50000","CVE-2023-53111","CVE-2023-53577","CVE-2024-35864","CVE-2024-35939","CVE-2024-41013","CVE-2024-44934","CVE-2024-50063","CVE-2024-53095","CVE-2024-53168","CVE-2025-39797","CVE-2025-39965","CVE-2025-40075","CVE-2025-68188","CVE-2026-31527","CVE-2026-43329","CVE-2026-46119","CVE-2026-46266","CVE-2026-52956","CVE-2026-53091","CVE-2026-53120","CVE-2026-53131","CVE-2026-64109","CVE-2026-64424","CVE-2026-68399","CVE-2026-68426","CVE-2026-72389","CVE-2026-74289","CVE-2026-74550","CVE-2026-89537","CVE-2026-89550","CVE-2026-89564","CVE-2026-90111","CVE-2026-98364","CVE-2026-98432","CVE-2026-99999"],"summary":"Fix of 34 CVEs","details":"   * Update to upstream stable Linux 5.10.272 (from 5.10.271).\n   * Bump kernel ABI to 51: ship the ELS kernel as 5.10.0-51-*, distinct from\n     the prior 5.10.0-50.\n   * CVE-2021-47200\n     - drm/prime: Fix use after free in mmap with drm_gem_ttm_mmap\n       {CVE-2021-47200}\n   * CVE-2022-50000\n     - netfilter: flowtable: fix stuck flows on cleanup due to pending\n       work {CVE-2022-50000}\n   * CVE-2023-53111\n     - loop: Fix use-after-free issues {CVE-2023-53111}\n   * CVE-2023-53577\n     - bpf, cpumap: Make sure kthread is running before map update\n       returns {CVE-2023-53577}\n   * CVE-2024-35864\n     - smb: client: fix potential UAF in smb2_is_valid_lease_break()\n       {CVE-2024-35864}\n   * CVE-2024-35939\n     - dma-direct: Leak pages on dma_set_decrypted() failure\n       {CVE-2024-35939}\n   * CVE-2024-41013\n     - xfs: don't walk off the end of a directory data block\n       {CVE-2024-41013}\n   * CVE-2024-44934\n     - net: bridge: mcast: wait for previous gc cycles when removing port\n       {CVE-2024-44934}\n   * CVE-2024-50063\n     - bpf: Prevent tail call between progs attached to different hooks\n       {CVE-2024-50063}\n   * CVE-2024-53095\n     - net: make sock_inuse_add() available {CVE-2024-53095}\n     - smb: client: Fix use-after-free of network namespace.\n       {CVE-2024-53095}\n   * CVE-2024-53168\n     - sunrpc: fix one UAF issue caused by sunrpc kernel tcp socket\n       {CVE-2024-53168}\n   * CVE-2025-39797\n     - xfrm: Duplicate SPI Handling {CVE-2025-39797}\n   * CVE-2025-39965\n     - xfrm: xfrm_alloc_spi shouldn't use 0 as SPI {CVE-2025-39965}\n   * CVE-2025-40075\n     - net: dst: introduce dst->dev_rcu {CVE-2025-40075}\n     - tcp_metrics: use dst_dev_net_rcu() {CVE-2025-40075}\n   * CVE-2025-68188\n     - tcp: use dst_dev_rcu() in tcp_fastopen_active_disable_ofo_check()\n       {CVE-2025-68188}\n   * CVE-2026-31527\n     - driver core: platform: use generic driver_override infrastructure\n       {CVE-2026-31527}\n   * CVE-2026-43329\n     - netfilter: flowtable: separate replace, destroy and stats to\n       different workqueues {CVE-2026-43329}\n     - netfilter: flowtable: pass flowtable to nf_flow_table_iterate()\n       {CVE-2026-43329}\n     - netfilter: flowtable: add function to invoke garbage collection\n       immediately {CVE-2026-43329}\n     - netfilter: flowtable: strictly check for maximum number of actions\n       {CVE-2026-43329}\n   * CVE-2026-46119\n     - libceph: Fix slab-out-of-bounds access in auth message processing\n       {CVE-2026-46119}\n   * CVE-2026-46266\n     - inet: RAW sockets using IPPROTO_RAW MUST drop incoming ICMP\n       {CVE-2026-46266}\n   * CVE-2026-52956\n     - libceph: Fix potential out-of-bounds access in __ceph_x_decrypt()\n       {CVE-2026-52956}\n   * CVE-2026-53091\n     - net: pull headers in qdisc_pkt_len_segs_init() {CVE-2026-53091}\n     - xfrm: Don't clobber inner headers when already set\n       {CVE-2026-53091}\n   * CVE-2026-53120\n     - PCI: use generic driver_override infrastructure {CVE-2026-53120}\n   * CVE-2026-53131\n     - netfilter: require Ethernet MAC header before using eth_hdr()\n       {CVE-2026-53131}\n   * CVE-2026-64109\n     - af_unix: Fix UAF read of tail->len in unix_stream_data_wait()\n       {CVE-2026-64109}\n   * CVE-2026-64424\n     - netpoll: fix a use-after-free on shutdown path {CVE-2026-64424}\n   * CVE-2026-68399\n     - bpf: Fix UAF in sock clone early bailouts {CVE-2026-68399}\n   * CVE-2026-68426\n     - xfrm: fix stale skb->prev after async crypto steals a GSO segment\n       {CVE-2026-68426}\n   * CVE-2026-72389\n     - bridge: stp: Fix a potential use-after-free when deleting a bridge\n       {CVE-2026-72389}\n   * CVE-2026-74289\n     - ipv4: fib: Don't dump dying fib_info in fib_leaf_notify().\n       {CVE-2026-74289}\n   * CVE-2026-74550\n     - net: do not send ICMP/NDISC Redirects when peer allocation fails\n       {CVE-2026-74550}\n   * CVE-2026-89537\n     - SUNRPC: Reject short RFC 4121 MIC tokens in gss_krb5_verify_mic_v2\n       {CVE-2026-89537}\n   * CVE-2026-89550\n     - SUNRPC: svcauth_gss: enforce krb5 token minimum length\n       {CVE-2026-89550}\n   * CVE-2026-89564\n     - ip: orphan prefetched skbs before multicast forwarding\n       {CVE-2026-89564}\n   * CVE-2026-90111\n     - ip6mr: do not clone dst in ip6mr_cache_report() {CVE-2026-90111}\n   * CVE-2026-98364\n     - xfrm: hold net_device reference under RCU in bundle creation\n       {CVE-2026-98364}\n   * CVE-2026-98432\n     - ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period\n       {CVE-2026-98432}\n   * CVE-2026-99999\n     - ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum\n       {CVE-2026-99999}\n   * Miscellaneous upstream changes\n     - netfilter: nfnetlink_queue: unbreak SCTP traffic\n     - Linux 5.10.272\n     - driver core: generalize driver_override in struct device\n     - hwmon: axi-fan: don't use driver_override as IRQ name\n     - netfilter: nf_tables: fix bidirectional offload regression","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bpftool","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/bpftool?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"